     "explanation": "Deliberately silencing notifications and removing the phone during a scheduled deep-work block is the essence of a zone of silence: you summon technology when you need it and dismiss it when you do not. Keeping all notifications on lets the device master your attention, and reacting only when it buzzes is still letting the phone set the rhythm. Deleting everything is the opposite error, throwing away a wonderful servant. Tracy wants intentional control, not total rejection.",
